  "pages": {
    "zh": {
      "overview": "# tool-common\n\n`tool-common` 负责跨领域、环境无关的 Tool Plane 业务能力；这些能力不自然归属于某个具体网络领域 owner。首项准入能力是 `subject.identity.lookup@v1`，用于把用户看到的名字或别名解析成逻辑 subject 和当前环境里的执行身份。\n\n最常见的例子：\n\n```text\n\"UE-B\"\n  ↓\nsubjectRef = receiver-b\n5gc.supi   = 001010000000002\n```\n\n它不负责 UE 注册、PDU Session、QoS、PFCP 等 5GC 状态；这些仍由 `env-5gc-sim` 或真实 5GC Provider 负责。\n\nRuntime 只访问 Provider listener 的只读接口。配置和 reset 走单独的 Control listener，不会暴露成 Agent Tool。\n",
      "subjectIdentity": "# Subject Identity\n\n## 查什么\n\n`subject.identity.lookup@v1` 接收一个用户可见的 name / alias，例如 `UE-B`，返回：\n\n- `subjectRef`：逻辑 subject；\n- `identities`：当前环境下的执行身份；\n- `mappingRevision`：这次结果来自哪一版映射；\n- `provenance`：配置摘要和 entry 数量。\n\nv1 当前要求 `5gc.supi`，`5gc.imsi` 可选，但如果存在必须和 SUPI 一致。\n\n## 结果\n\nLookup 本身成功执行时 HTTP 都返回 200，业务结果看 `status`：\n\n- `RESOLVED`：唯一匹配；\n- `NOT_FOUND`：没有匹配；\n- `AMBIGUOUS`：匹配到多个 subject，需要上层澄清。\n\n`NOT_FOUND` 和 `AMBIGUOUS` 不是 HTTP 错误。\n\n## 匹配规则\n\n匹配是确定性的：\n\n- 输入先 TrimSpace；\n- 之后按大小写敏感的精确匹配；\n- 不做模糊匹配、前缀匹配或 first-match；\n- 多个 subject 命中同一个 name / alias 时返回 `AMBIGUOUS`。\n\n## Revision\n\n映射修改必须推进 `mappingRevision`。调用者可以带 `expectedRevision` 做 fence，旧 revision 会 fail closed。\n",
      "boundaries": "# 职责边界\n\n| 事情 | Owner |\n| --- | --- |\n| 用户名 / alias → logical subject / execution identity | `tool-common` |\n| 模拟 5GC 注册、PDU Session、QoS、PFCP | `env-5gc-sim` |\n| 真实 5GC 接入 | `env-5gc-real` |\n| ProviderBinding、Outcome、Reconcile | `ca-runtime` |\n| Agent-facing MCP Tool | `tool-mcp-gw` |\n| 环境生命周期与可信 provisioning | `ca-lab` |\n\n两个 listener 职责互斥：\n\n- **Provider**：`POST /v1/subject-identities/lookup`，以及本 listener 的 `/openapi.yaml` 和 `/docs/`。\n- **Control**：Managed Node 操作、受信任的 identity configure/reset，以及本 listener 的 `/openapi.yaml` 和 `/docs/`。\n\nProviderBinding 是 capability-binding authority。Control route 不进入 Runtime Toolset。Managed Node drain 保留在 Control，并等待已准入工作完成后再报告成功。\n"
    },
    "en": {
      "overview": "# tool-common\n\n`tool-common` owns cross-domain / environment-neutral Tool Plane business capabilities that do not naturally belong to one concrete network-domain owner. Its first admitted capability is `subject.identity.lookup@v1`: resolving a user-visible name or alias into a logical subject and the execution identities for the current environment.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n\"UE-B\"\n  ↓\nsubjectRef = receiver-b\n5gc.supi   = 001010000000002\n```\n\nIt does not own 5GC registration, PDU sessions, QoS, PFCP, or other network-domain state. Those remain with `env-5gc-sim` or the real 5GC Provider.\n\nRuntime uses the read-only Provider listener. Provisioning and reset use a separate trusted Control listener and are not Agent tools.\n",
      "subjectIdentity": "# Subject Identity\n\n## Lookup\n\n`subject.identity.lookup@v1` accepts a user-visible name or alias such as `UE-B` and returns:\n\n- `subjectRef`: the logical subject;\n- `identities`: execution identities for the current environment;\n- `mappingRevision`: the mapping revision used for the result;\n- `provenance`: configuration digest and entry count.\n\nv1 requires `5gc.supi`. `5gc.imsi` is optional, but must be equal to SUPI when present.\n\n## Results\n\nA successfully executed lookup returns HTTP 200. The semantic result is in `status`:\n\n- `RESOLVED`: exactly one match;\n- `NOT_FOUND`: no match;\n- `AMBIGUOUS`: multiple subjects match and the caller must clarify.\n\n`NOT_FOUND` and `AMBIGUOUS` are not HTTP errors.\n\n## Matching\n\nMatching is deterministic:\n\n- trim the input first;\n- exact case-sensitive match afterwards;\n- no fuzzy, prefix, or first-match behavior;\n- a shared name/alias across subjects returns `AMBIGUOUS`.\n\n## Revision\n\nMapping changes must advance `mappingRevision`. Trusted callers can use `expectedRevision` as a fence; stale revisions fail closed.\n",
      "boundaries": "# Boundaries\n\n| Concern | Owner |\n| --- | --- |\n| user-visible name / alias → logical subject / execution identity | `tool-common` |\n| simulated 5GC registration, PDU sessions, QoS, PFCP | `env-5gc-sim` |\n| real 5GC integration | `env-5gc-real` |\n| ProviderBinding, Outcome, Reconcile | `ca-runtime` |\n| Agent-facing MCP tools | `tool-mcp-gw` |\n| environment lifecycle and trusted provisioning | `ca-lab` |\n\nThe listeners have disjoint responsibilities:\n\n- **Provider**: `POST /v1/subject-identities/lookup`, plus its own `/openapi.yaml` and `/docs/`.\n- **Control**: Managed Node operations, trusted identity configure/reset, and its own `/openapi.yaml` and `/docs/`.\n\nProviderBinding is capability-binding authority. Control routes do not enter the Runtime Toolset. Managed Node drain remains on Control and drains already admitted work before reporting success.\n"
    }
  },
